            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0476" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.156/132.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-01-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 25, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The following reply regarding bridge has been received from the Cuban Secretary
                    of State: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Since the bill in question has been enacted by Congress and approved by
                            the President, the latter has no means at his disposal for suspending
                            its effect; but he intends to defer its execution for a reasonable
                            period in the confident hope that the United States will promptly
                            complete its study of the matter and, if there are no objections to so
                            doing, communicate its findings to the Government of Cuba.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
